{"name":"Ginger Root Peel","hex":"#f0c48c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ginger","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The pungent aromatic rhizome of a tropical Asian herb, Zingiber officinale, used as a spice and as a stimulant and acarminative.","The plant that produces this rhizome."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a reddish-brown color.","Having hair or fur of this color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ginger"},{"term":"root","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The part of a plant, generally underground, that anchors and supports the plant body, absorbs and stores water and nutrients, and in some plants is able to perform vegetative reproduction.","A root vegetable."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grow roots; to enter the earth, as roots; to take root and begin to grow.","To prepare, oversee, or otherwise cause the rooting of cuttings."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/root"},{"term":"peel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To remove the skin or outer covering of.","To remove something from the outer or top layer of."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The skin or outer layer of a fruit, vegetable, etc.","The action of peeling away from a formation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ginger","blocks":[{"text":"Ginger is a flowering plant whose rhizome, ginger root or ginger, is widely used as a spice and a folk medicine. It is an herbaceous perennial that grows annual pseudostems about one meter tall, bearing narrow leaf blades. The inflorescences bear flowers having pale yellow petals with purple edges, and arise directly from the rhizome on separate shoots."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Koeh-146-no_text.jpg/330px-Koeh-146-no_text.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ginger","wikidata":"Q35625"},{"titl